Risks Related Ownership of Our Common Stock

An active trading market for our common stock may not continue to develop or be sustained.

Prior to the IPO, there was no public market for our common stock. An active trading market for our shares may not continue to develop or be sustained. The lack of an active market may impair the value of your shares, your ability to sell your shares at the time you wish to sell them and the prices that you may obtain for your shares. Further, an inactive trading market for our shares may also impair our ability to raise capital by selling shares of our common stock or enter into strategic partnerships and transactions by issuing our shares of common stock as consideration.

The trading price of our common stock may be volatile, and you could lose all or part of your investment.

